// `@linkName` renames a SYMBOL, and an ordinary `fn` has none of its own: kama chooses its C name
// (scope-prefixed) and nothing outside the program links against it. `expose` is how a function gets a
// fixed symbol; the attribute then names it.
@linkName("helper") fn int32 helper() { return 1; }
fn int32 main() { return helper(); }
